    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d503">

                <pb facs="0810" n="800" sameAs="frus:frus1946v10/pg800"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Marshall Mission Files, Lot 54–D270:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Colonel Marshall S. Carter to General Marshall </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-07-16">16 July 1946</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>94585. On 12 July, for your information, the Chinese Supply Commission placed
                    $5,500,000 in escrow with U. S. Maritime Commission, and signed an agreement
                    whereby “the use and possession” of the 10 SCALS Liberty ships was transferred
                    to the Chinese Government Copy of agreement<anchor n="74" xml:id="d503-f1"/>
                    follows by courier. Policies for final sale to foreign governments not yet
                    agreed by Maritime Commission.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
